{"v": 1, "key": "cu-cu12", "cards": [{"id": "u5.t.fungus", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">FUN<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">gus<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"fungus\" data-audio=\"audio/fungus.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: fungus\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u5-fungus.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"533\" alt=\"Fly agaric mushrooms on a forest floor. The mushroom is only the fruiting body of a much larger fungus underground.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Fly agaric mushrooms on a forest floor. The mushroom is only the fruiting body of a much larger fungus underground.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">林地上的毒蝇伞。蘑菇只是地下更大真菌的子实体。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Holger Krisp · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fliegenpilz_fly_agaric_Amanita_muscaria.JPG\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"fungus\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Fungus<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">chitin wall,<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">absorbs food, no<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"84\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">photosynthesis<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"22\" width=\"90\" height=\"76\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"42\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Examples<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"60\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mushroom, mold,<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">yeast<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A eukaryote with a chitin cell wall that feeds by absorbing nutrients from its surroundings. Plural: fungi.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>真菌<\/b>：细胞壁含几丁质、靠吸收周围养分获取营养的真核生物，复数 fungi。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">fungus = Latin for mushroom.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">fungus 在拉丁语里是「蘑菇」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Can a fungus photosynthesize?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. It absorbs food from its surroundings.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u5.t.hypha", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">HY<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">pha<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"hypha\" data-tts=\"1\" aria-label=\"Listen: hypha\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u5-hypha.webp\" width=\"720\" height=\"540\" alt=\"Hyphae of the mold Penicillium under a microscope (bar = 100 micrometres).\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Hyphae of the mold Penicillium under a microscope (bar = 100 micrometres).<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">显微镜下青霉菌的菌丝（比例尺 = 100 微米）。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Y_tambe · <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Penicillium.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"hypha\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"60\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"35\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"85\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"25\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"50\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"80\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"100\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"45\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"38\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"112\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">one hypha = one thread<\/text><text x=\"150\" y=\"15\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"start\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">branching<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A thin thread of cells that forms the body of most fungi. Plural: hyphae.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>菌丝<\/b>：构成大多数真菌身体的细丝状细胞。复数 hyphae。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">hyphe = Greek for web.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">hyphe 在希腊语里是「网」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is a hypha?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">A thread-like filament that makes up a fungus.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u5.t.mycelium", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"sy\">my<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"st\">CE<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">li<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">um<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"mycelium\" data-audio=\"audio/mycelium.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: mycelium\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u5-mycelium.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"White mycelium spreading through soil and dead leaves under a mushroom.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">White mycelium spreading through soil and dead leaves under a mushroom.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">蘑菇下方在土壤和落叶间蔓延的白色菌丝体。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: The original uploader was Lex vB at Dutch Wikipedia. · <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mushroom%27s_roots_(myc%C3%A9lium).jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"mycelium\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"60\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"35\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"85\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"25\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"35\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"50\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"80\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"135\" y2=\"100\" class=\"k\"/><line x1=\"40\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"45\" y2=\"45\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"85\" y1=\"48\" x2=\"80\" y2=\"38\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"20\" y2=\"30\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"20\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"15\" y2=\"90\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"60\" x2=\"60\" y2=\"95\" class=\"\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"85\" x2=\"90\" y2=\"108\" class=\"\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"14\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mycelium = a web of hyphae<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A mass of branching hyphae that makes up the main body of a fungus.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>菌丝体<\/b>：由许多分枝菌丝构成的真菌主体。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">myco = fungus.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">myco = 真菌。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What is the main body of most fungi?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">The mycelium.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u5.t.chitin", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">CHI<\/span><i class=\"dot\">·<\/i><span class=\"sy\">tin<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"chitin\" data-audio=\"audio/chitin.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: chitin\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"chitin\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"90\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"51\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Fungal wall<\/text><text x=\"51\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">chitin<\/text><rect x=\"104\" y=\"34\" width=\"90\" height=\"52\" rx=\"8\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"149\" y=\"54\" font-size=\"11\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Plant wall<\/text><text x=\"149\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">cellulose<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A tough, flexible material that forms the cell walls of fungi. It also makes insect shells.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>几丁质<\/b>：构成真菌细胞壁的坚韧有韧性的物质，也构成昆虫外壳。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">chitin ~ &quot;tunic&quot; in Greek.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">chitin 在希腊语里近似「外衣」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: What material is in fungal cell walls?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Chitin.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u5.t.spore", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">SPORE<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"spore\" data-audio=\"audio/spore.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: spore\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u5-spore.webp\" width=\"616\" height=\"800\" alt=\"A puffball mushroom. When it is ripe, a puff of millions of spores comes out of the hole on top.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">A puffball mushroom. When it is ripe, a puff of millions of spores comes out of the hole on top.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">马勃。成熟后，顶部的小孔会喷出数以百万计的孢子。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Daniel Ullrich, Threedots · <a href=\"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Single_lycoperdon_perlatum.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"spore\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Spore<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">lands on<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">food<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"53.6\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Germinates<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"62.8\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">(hyphae<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"72\" font-size=\"8.0\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">grow)<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">New<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mycelium<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A tiny reproductive cell that can grow into a new organism without joining another cell.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>孢子<\/b>：微小的繁殖细胞，不需要与其他细胞结合就能长成新个体。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">spora = seed in Greek.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">spora 在希腊语里是「种子」。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Do spores need fertilization to grow?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. A spore can grow on its own.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u5.t.mold", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">MOLD<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"mold\" data-audio=\"audio/mold.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: mold\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u5-mold.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"600\" alt=\"Black bread mold (Rhizopus). The fine threads are hyphae; the black dots are sporangia full of spores.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Black bread mold (Rhizopus). The fine threads are hyphae; the black dots are sporangia full of spores.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">黑面包霉（根霉）。细丝是菌丝，黑点是装满孢子的孢子囊。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: WDKeeper · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY-SA 4.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rhizopus_stolonifer4.JPG\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"mold\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"40\" y=\"60\" width=\"120\" height=\"30\" rx=\"4\" class=\"f6\"/><path d=\"M50 60 Q60 35 70 60 Q85 30 95 60 Q110 38 120 60 Q135 32 150 60\" class=\"s\"/><line x1=\"70\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"70\" y2=\"30\" class=\"\"/><circle cx=\"70\" cy=\"26\" r=\"4\" class=\"f2\"/><line x1=\"100\" y1=\"46\" x2=\"100\" y2=\"26\" class=\"\"/><circle cx=\"100\" cy=\"22\" r=\"4\" class=\"f2\"/><line x1=\"130\" y1=\"50\" x2=\"130\" y2=\"30\" class=\"\"/><circle cx=\"130\" cy=\"26\" r=\"4\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"108\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">mold on bread: hyphae and spores<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"12\" font-size=\"9\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">sporangia on stalks<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A fungus that grows as fuzzy masses of hyphae on food or damp surfaces.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>霉菌<\/b>：在食物或潮湿表面形成绒毛状菌丝团的真菌。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">mold on bread is a living network.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">面包上的霉是活的菌丝网。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Is bread mold a plant?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">No. It is a fungus.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}, {"id": "u5.t.yeast", "f": "<div class=\"bt-front\"><div class=\"term-line\"><span class=\"term big\" lang=\"en\"><span class=\"st\">YEAST<\/span><\/span><button type=\"button\" class=\"say\" data-say=\"yeast\" data-audio=\"audio/yeast.m4a\" aria-label=\"Listen: yeast\" title=\"Listen\"><span aria-hidden=\"true\">🔊<\/span><\/button><\/div><\/div>", "b": "<div class=\"bt-back\"><figure class=\"photo\"><img src=\"photos/u5-yeast.webp\" width=\"800\" height=\"517\" alt=\"Yeast cells under an electron microscope (bar = 5 micrometres). Some are budding.\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"><figcaption><span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">Yeast cells under an electron microscope (bar = 5 micrometres). Some are budding.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">电子显微镜下的酵母细胞（比例尺 = 5 微米），有些正在出芽。<\/span><small class=\"cred\">Photo: Mogana Das Murtey and Patchamuthu Ramasamy · <a href=\"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0\" rel=\"license noopener\">CC BY 3.0<\/a> · <a href=\"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Saccharomyces_cerevisiae_SEM.jpg\" rel=\"noopener\">Wikimedia Commons<\/a><\/small><\/figcaption><\/figure><svg class=\"pic\" viewBox=\"0 0 200 120\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"yeast\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" fill=\"none\"><rect x=\"6\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f1\"/><text x=\"32\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Yeast<\/text><text x=\"32\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">cell<\/text><line x1=\"59.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"73.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"73.0,60.0 68.5,62.2 68.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"74\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f2\"/><text x=\"100\" y=\"57.9\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Bud<\/text><text x=\"100\" y=\"69.1\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">forms<\/text><line x1=\"127.0\" y1=\"60.0\" x2=\"141.0\" y2=\"60.0\"/><polygon points=\"141.0,60.0 136.5,62.2 136.5,57.8\" fill=\"currentColor\"/><rect x=\"142\" y=\"34\" width=\"52\" height=\"52\" rx=\"6\" class=\"f3\"/><text x=\"168\" y=\"52.3\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">Bud<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"63.5\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">breaks<\/text><text x=\"168\" y=\"74.7\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke=\"none\">off<\/text><\/svg><p class=\"def\"><span lang=\"en\">A single-celled fungus that reproduces by budding and can ferment sugar.<\/span><\/p><p class=\"zhdef\"><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\"><b>酵母<\/b>：单细胞真菌，靠出芽繁殖，能发酵糖。<\/span><\/p><p class=\"hook\"><b>🧠<\/b> <span class=\"en\" lang=\"en\">one of the few common single-celled fungi.<\/span><span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">常见真菌里少有的单细胞种类。<\/span><\/p><details class=\"chk\"><summary><span lang=\"en\">Quick check: Is yeast single-celled or multicellular?<\/span><\/summary><p class=\"chk-a\" lang=\"en\">Single-celled.<\/p><\/details><\/div>"}], "quiz": [{"id": "cu.q.u5.t.fungus", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A eukaryote with a chitin cell wall that feeds by absorbing nutrients from its surroundings. Plural: fungi.”<\/i>", "opts": ["mycelium", "mycosis", "basidium", "fungus"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>fungus<\/b>: A eukaryote with a chitin cell wall that feeds by absorbing nutrients from its surroundings. Plural: fungi. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">真菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u5.t.hypha", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A thin thread of cells that forms the body of most fungi. Plural: hyphae.”<\/i>", "opts": ["club fungi", "penicillin", "yeast", "hypha"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>hypha<\/b>: A thin thread of cells that forms the body of most fungi. Plural: hyphae. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">菌丝<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u5.t.mycelium", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A mass of branching hyphae that makes up the main body of a fungus.”<\/i>", "opts": ["septum", "budding", "club fungi", "mycelium"], "a": 3, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>mycelium<\/b>: A mass of branching hyphae that makes up the main body of a fungus. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">菌丝体<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u5.t.chitin", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A tough, flexible material that forms the cell walls of fungi. It also makes insect shells.”<\/i>", "opts": ["mycosis", "chitin", "fungus", "gills"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>chitin<\/b>: A tough, flexible material that forms the cell walls of fungi. It also makes insect shells. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">几丁质<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u5.t.spore", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A tiny reproductive cell that can grow into a new organism without joining another cell.”<\/i>", "opts": ["conidia", "spore", "mushroom", "mold"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>spore<\/b>: A tiny reproductive cell that can grow into a new organism without joining another cell. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">孢子<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u5.t.mold", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A fungus that grows as fuzzy masses of hyphae on food or damp surfaces.”<\/i>", "opts": ["hypha", "mold", "mycorrhiza", "fermentation"], "a": 1, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>mold<\/b>: A fungus that grows as fuzzy masses of hyphae on food or damp surfaces. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">霉菌<\/span>", "whys": null}, {"id": "cu.q.u5.t.yeast", "q": "Which term matches this definition?<br><i>“A single-celled fungus that reproduces by budding and can ferment sugar.”<\/i>", "opts": ["mycosis", "fragmentation", "yeast", "pioneer species"], "a": 2, "hint": null, "ans": null, "why": "<b>yeast<\/b>: A single-celled fungus that reproduces by budding and can ferment sugar. <span class=\"zh\" lang=\"zh-Hans\">酵母<\/span>", "whys": null}]}